  "@type": "Capability",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Thermal energy transfer between two fluid streams separated by a solid wall, governed by Q = U x A x LMTD. Three principal configurations: shell-and-tube (handles 300 bar and 600C, 70% of industrial installations), plate (highest coefficient 3,000-7,000 W/m2-K, compact, limited to 25 bar and 200C), and double-pipe (simplest, small duties). Proper heat integration using hot process streams to heat cold ones reduces plant energy consumption by 30-50%. Counter-current flow maximizes the log mean temperature difference. Enables distillation condensers/reboilers, reactor jacket heating, feed preheating, and waste heat recovery across every chemical process.",
  "early_win": false,
